# Rust workspace build output
/target
/src-tauri/gen/schemas

# Claude Code local session state — machine/user-specific, never shared.
# Skills are the exception: they are checked-in tooling, not session state, and
# an agent working anywhere in the repo discovers them from here. Ignoring the
# contents rather than the directory is what lets one child back in — git will
# not descend into an excluded directory, so `!.claude/skills/` alone would not
# work.
.claude/*
!.claude/skills/

# Comparison build of ghostty main, used only by the port's parity checks.
# 5 MB artifact, never loaded by the app — see the README kept beside it.
src/lib/ghostty/main/vendor-main/*.wasm
src/lib/ghostty/main/vendor-main/*.h
